WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.070 --> 00:00:06.399
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie and there’s
a bunch of Marvel news lately mostly Ant-Man

00:00:06.399 --> 00:00:11.969
and Doctor Strange but they just officially
said they’re not doing origin stories for

00:00:11.969 --> 00:00:15.379
any new characters.

00:00:15.379 --> 00:00:18.580
This video will mostly be about how that’s
going to affect the future of the Marvel Universe

00:00:18.580 --> 00:00:22.109
but there is some cool info about the Doctor
Strange movie and Ant-Man started filming.

00:00:22.109 --> 00:00:23.619
So I’ve got lots of cool behind the scenes
stuff to break down.

00:00:23.619 --> 00:00:28.820
Starting with biggest stuff first No More
Origin Stories, Here’s what happened:

00:00:28.820 --> 00:00:33.580
There are currently 30 comic book films from
all the studios being released between now

00:00:33.580 --> 00:00:34.780
and 2020.

00:00:34.780 --> 00:00:38.829
That’s 30 tent pole big budget movies in
6 years.

00:00:38.829 --> 00:00:40.570
It’s totally crazy.

00:00:40.570 --> 00:00:43.950
And if you look at the model Marvel, Warner
Brothers, Fox, Sony use for developing new

00:00:43.950 --> 00:00:44.950
IP.

00:00:44.950 --> 00:00:50.289
That’s intellectual property, meaning new
characters, dropping Origin Stories totally

00:00:50.289 --> 00:00:52.149
makes sense.

00:00:52.149 --> 00:00:56.219
Doctor Strange is the first Marvel movie that’s
going to adhere to this rule.

00:00:56.219 --> 00:01:03.910
It’s not an industry thing, Marvel is the
only group that has said no more origin stories.

00:01:03.910 --> 00:01:08.590
This is what used to happen when a studio
had a character or a team and wanted to start

00:01:08.590 --> 00:01:09.770
a new franchise.

00:01:09.770 --> 00:01:10.850
Like Avengers.

00:01:10.850 --> 00:01:17.910
You have your origin story movie, then the
sequel with more villains, the another sequel

00:01:17.910 --> 00:01:23.380
where the hero crashes and burns emotionally,
then a team up.

00:01:23.380 --> 00:01:27.049
It’s a formula that almost every major comic
book movie has followed.

00:01:27.049 --> 00:01:31.360
And it worked at first, but it’s been a
long time since Tim Burton’s Batman films

00:01:31.360 --> 00:01:32.520
and the original spider-man trilogy.

00:01:32.520 --> 00:01:34.229
Even since the first Iron Man movie.

00:01:34.229 --> 00:01:38.770
Now the number of new characters is rising
exponentially.

00:01:38.770 --> 00:01:44.909
Marvel, and I’m sure the other studios,
feel that people will get sick of the formula.

00:01:44.909 --> 00:01:49.259
After 20 plus origin story movies, people
just won’t care as much anymore.

00:01:49.259 --> 00:01:53.810
So in response, starting with Doctor Strange,
Marvel will no longer introduce new comic

00:01:53.810 --> 00:01:56.450
book characters in Origin Stories.

00:01:56.450 --> 00:01:58.620
What does that mean?

00:01:58.620 --> 00:02:04.090
When we see the Doctor Strange movie, he’ll
already be Sorcerer Supreme at the beginning

00:02:04.090 --> 00:02:06.460
of the movie.

00:02:06.460 --> 00:02:11.180
Right now Doctor Strange has a director named
Scott Derrickson and a writer Jon Spaihts,

00:02:11.180 --> 00:02:13.670
he’s the guy who wrote Prometheus for Ridley
Scott.

00:02:13.670 --> 00:02:21.330
Here’s a quick history of that Movie at
Marvel.

00:02:21.330 --> 00:02:24.780
They’ve had an in-house script for a long
time.

00:02:24.780 --> 00:02:28.250
Marvel hires teams of writers to comb through
their catalog of characters and try to develop

00:02:28.250 --> 00:02:30.580
scripts for characters that haven’t been
in the movies yet.

00:02:30.580 --> 00:02:33.320
It’s an in house writing program they’ve
had for a while.

00:02:33.320 --> 00:02:36.330
It’s how Guardians of the Galaxy turned
into a movie.

00:02:36.330 --> 00:02:41.110
A writer inside the program named Nicole Perlman
thought that Guardians would make a good movie,

00:02:41.110 --> 00:02:45.400
wrote a script, marvel liked that script so
much they sent that script to directors till

00:02:45.400 --> 00:02:47.980
James Gunn accepted the offer.

00:02:47.980 --> 00:02:49.670
He re-wrote the original script.

00:02:49.670 --> 00:02:52.890
And the same thing is happening on the Doctor
Strange movie right now.

00:02:52.890 --> 00:02:55.710
Scott Derrickson and the writer Jon Spaights
are re-writing the original script.

00:02:55.710 --> 00:03:00.090
The old one was written to be an origin story.

00:03:00.090 --> 00:03:06.040
Their new script they’re working on will
be more like the structure of Batman Begins

00:03:06.040 --> 00:03:07.330
or Man of Steel.

00:03:07.330 --> 00:03:09.680
It will still deal with origins, but only
in flashback.

00:03:09.680 --> 00:03:16.160
Isn’t it funny to think that Marvel is taking
a cue from Christopher Nolan?

00:03:16.160 --> 00:03:20.484
That’s not really going on, Batman Begins
is just a good example of a Movie that tells

00:03:20.484 --> 00:03:23.990
an origin story without being a true origin
story in a linear way.

00:03:23.990 --> 00:03:27.140
Even Guardians of the Galaxy already skipped
a lot of the characters origins.

00:03:27.140 --> 00:03:31.730
You see Star-Lord as a child for about 5 minutes
before it picks up with him as a fully actualized

00:03:31.730 --> 00:03:33.180
scoundrel slash hero.

00:03:33.180 --> 00:03:38.280
Let me know what you guys think about this,
it’s huge thing for Marvel to say, no more

00:03:38.280 --> 00:03:39.280
origin stories.

00:03:39.280 --> 00:03:43.060
Do you think it’s better for them to just
pick right up with the action without first

00:03:43.060 --> 00:03:54.040
seeing characters learn how to use their powers?

00:03:54.040 --> 00:03:59.190
I think given the 30 films we’ve got coming
it will be a welcome change of pace.

00:03:59.190 --> 00:04:03.070
And they can still do origin stories with
digital content.

00:04:03.070 --> 00:04:04.070
That’s stuff that only gets released on
the web.

00:04:04.070 --> 00:04:05.770
Or short stories they make and then release
as DVD bonus content.

00:04:05.770 --> 00:04:07.340
Like the Marvel One Shots.

00:04:07.340 --> 00:04:12.320
That original Doctor Strange script wasn’t
terrible.

00:04:12.320 --> 00:04:17.120
It was written by the guy who wrote Sahara,
that Matthew McConaughey movie.

00:04:17.120 --> 00:04:19.370
You can insert all the jokes you want.

00:04:19.370 --> 00:04:24.570
But it featured Baron Mordo as the main villain
and followed the original comic book origin

00:04:24.570 --> 00:04:25.570
story pretty faithfully.

00:04:25.570 --> 00:04:29.290
There was an animated movie that did a version
of the origin story too with a few changes.

00:04:29.290 --> 00:04:32.350
If you haven’t seen it, it’s as good as
Marvel’s other animated movies.

00:04:32.350 --> 00:04:35.170
It’s streaming on Netflix Instant so you
can watch it there.

00:04:35.170 --> 00:04:39.690
And you may have heard the rumors about the
bigger actors being considered for the movie.

00:04:39.690 --> 00:04:44.180
They settled on one, but because that person
didn’t sign the contract before Comic Con,

00:04:44.180 --> 00:04:45.220
they didn’t announce anything.

00:04:45.220 --> 00:04:48.720
The biggest last minute rumors were Joaquin
Phoenix and Jared Leto.

00:04:48.720 --> 00:04:51.610
Benedict Cumberbatch made some jokes during
his panel too.

00:04:51.610 --> 00:04:54.320
He’d be my pick and he was in talks with
the studio.

00:04:54.320 --> 00:04:59.650
But he’s doing Hamlet for most of the period
next year when they’d be filming the movie.

00:04:59.650 --> 00:05:03.280
So I don’t think he’ll be Doctor Strange.

00:05:03.280 --> 00:05:06.990
Picking someone like Joaquin Phoenix is another
good reason to ditch the origin story.

00:05:06.990 --> 00:05:11.350
Doctor Strange is such a crazy character,
I could totally see him as this haunted sorcerer.

00:05:11.350 --> 00:05:15.020
But I don’t think he’d work as well as
Stephen Strange the Doctor.

00:05:15.020 --> 00:05:19.590
It’s also possible that the actor they want
hated the origin story script and that’s

00:05:19.590 --> 00:05:21.120
part of what is holding things up.

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:30.000
Based on their release date they have to cast
someone and start filming by next year.

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:37.720
So they’ll have to find their man in the
next couple of months.

00:05:37.720 --> 00:05:39.320
Speaking of shooting on to Ant-Man.

00:05:39.320 --> 00:05:43.840
They just started filming this week in San
Francisco and released a picture, this is

00:05:43.840 --> 00:05:46.390
a day one on the set picture.

00:05:46.390 --> 00:05:52.660
Just to compare, the new Fantastic Four movie
has finished filming and hasn’t released

00:05:52.660 --> 00:05:57.850
any images or promo art.

00:05:57.850 --> 00:06:07.100
It shows Paul Rudd as Scott Lang in a van
down by the river.

00:06:07.100 --> 00:06:11.889
The thought is that they changed the previous
script and are being more faithful to the

00:06:11.889 --> 00:06:13.260
comic book origins.

00:06:13.260 --> 00:06:17.020
The original script had him working at Hank
Pym’s company along with Yellow Jacket.

00:06:17.020 --> 00:06:19.460
They explained some of the details in the
comic con panel.

00:06:19.460 --> 00:06:23.900
I’ll link that video at the end of this
and in the description.

00:06:23.900 --> 00:06:28.330
Now it seems like Scott Lang is going to be
a common criminal stealing stuff to pay for

00:06:28.330 --> 00:06:29.750
his daughter’s medical bills.

00:06:29.750 --> 00:06:33.710
He was always a brilliant scientist, he just
became a common criminal to help his family

00:06:33.710 --> 00:06:34.710
survive.

00:06:34.710 --> 00:06:39.000
He ended up stealing the Ant-Man costume and
eventually Hank Pym passed the torch.

00:06:39.000 --> 00:06:43.700
I did a whole other video explaining the origin
of the character and how he ended up with

00:06:43.700 --> 00:06:45.720
the avengers I’ll link in the description
too.

00:06:45.720 --> 00:06:51.669
It’s pretty straight forward as an origin
story, he started in Avengers 181 in 1979

00:06:51.669 --> 00:06:56.650
and officially took the mantle of Ant-Man
in Marvel Premiere 47 later that year.

00:06:56.650 --> 00:06:58.750
So you should definitely check those comics
out.

00:06:58.750 --> 00:07:04.950
He’s also featured in the 2012 Fantastic
Four comic Matt Fraction wrote.

00:07:04.950 --> 00:07:08.610
That’s just a funny coincidence that I compared
the Fantastic Four reboot and Ant-Man’s

00:07:08.610 --> 00:07:10.639
comparative open-ness with images from the
set.

00:07:10.639 --> 00:07:14.571
I’d really love to see Paul Rudd in a future
Avengers movie, that probably won’t happen

00:07:14.571 --> 00:07:16.020
during Avengers 2.

00:07:16.020 --> 00:07:17.919
He was part of the team in the comics.

00:07:17.919 --> 00:07:21.360
Maybe by the time they get around to Avengers
3 he’ll show up on the roster.

00:07:21.360 --> 00:07:26.250
Marvel will be changing the Avengers roster
between Age of Ultron and the third movie.

00:07:26.250 --> 00:07:30.530
Too many new characters will be around for
them to not include them.

00:07:30.530 --> 00:07:32.800
And actors will start leaving.

00:07:32.800 --> 00:07:37.650
I have no idea how long Samuel L Jackson and
Robert Downey Jr will stay with the studio,

00:07:37.650 --> 00:07:39.890
but they are currently the senior members.

00:07:39.890 --> 00:07:44.610
That’s a good question to end on, which
core Avenger do you think will be the first

00:07:44.610 --> 00:07:45.770
to leave their role.

00:07:45.770 --> 00:07:48.510
Like stop being their character in the movies?

00:07:48.510 --> 00:07:52.710
My bet is still on Robert Downey Jr, he’s
currently only signed for one more movie and

00:07:52.710 --> 00:07:53.710
that’s Avengers 3.

00:07:53.710 --> 00:07:58.320
That was his new deal, Avengers 2 and 3 and
that’s it.

00:07:58.320 --> 00:07:59.440
Unless they sign a new contract.

